return [====[iv class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 80</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_arc_recovery" data-title="Arc Recovery"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Arc Recovery</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_ARC_RECOVERY"><h3>Arc Recovery</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / magic_pool</p><p>Defeating an AI hostile with a Magic-tagged damage event restores 5 Magic, subject to one 2.0-second per-actor internal cooldown and the universal 100-Magic ceiling.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and Magic-using AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 81</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_arcane_disruption_proc" data-title="Disruptor"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Disruptor</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_ARCANE_PROC_1"><h3>Disruptor</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13</p><p>Sets ArcaneDisruptionProcChance = 0.11. When an eligible physical=true, magical=false target-hit event damages a surviving target whose Arcane Shield is online, a successful proc forces exactly one post-damage Arcane Integrity save using the ordinary attacker-INT ArcaneBreakDC and defender-INT ArcaneIntegritySave formulas. This does not retag the underlying damage as magical. The physical hit remains ordinarily Feedback-eligible, and any Feedback resolution from that hit completes before this proc-created Arcane Integrity save. Magical hits do not roll this family because they already force Arcane Integrity saves automatically.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_ARCANE_PROC_2"><h3>Spellbreaker</h3><p class="requirement">INT 15 / requires Disruptor</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets ArcaneDisruptionProcChance = 0.22. When an eligible physical=true, magical=false target-hit event damages a surviving target whose Arcane Shield is online, a successful proc forces exactly one post-damage Arcane Integrity save using the ordinary attacker-INT ArcaneBreakDC and defender-INT ArcaneIntegritySave formulas. This does not retag the underlying damage as magical. The physical hit remains ordinarily Feedback-eligible, and any Feedback resolution from that hit completes before this proc-created Arcane Integrity save. Magical hits do not roll this family because they already force Arcane Integrity saves automatically.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_ARCANE_PROC_3"><h3>Nullifier</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / requires Spellbreaker</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets ArcaneDisruptionProcChance = 0.33. When an eligible physical=true, magical=false target-hit event damages a surviving target whose Arcane Shield is online, a successful proc forces exactly one post-damage Arcane Integrity save using the ordinary attacker-INT ArcaneBreakDC and defender-INT ArcaneIntegritySave formulas. This does not retag the underlying damage as magical. The physical hit remains ordinarily Feedback-eligible, and any Feedback resolution from that hit completes before this proc-created Arcane Integrity save. Magical hits do not roll this family because they already force Arcane Integrity saves automatically.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 82</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_backpedal" data-title="W,A,S,Deborah"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>W,A,S,Deborah</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_WAS_DEBORAH"><h3>W,A,S,Deborah</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Voluntary backward movement, including backward diagonals, is 25% faster. Composes with ordinary movement modes and map movement. Forward movement, pure strafing, jumping and forced motion are unchanged.</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 83</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_cloud_step" data-title="Cloud Step"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Cloud Step</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_CLOUD_STEP"><h3>Cloud Step</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13 / Magic pool</p><p>Once per airborne cycle, a fresh Space press may spend exactly 5 Magic for one additional voluntary jump. A valid Wall Jump with a remaining use has priority and leaves Cloud Step unused.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 84</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_extracurricular_activity" data-title="Extracurricular Activity"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Extracurricular Activity</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_EXTRACURRICULAR_ACTIVITY"><h3>Extracurricular Activity</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / unowned Magic content</p><p>Immediately grants one deterministic distinct canonical Magic content without replacing later scheduled grants.</p><p class="actors">Cooperative Heroes only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 85</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_feedback_loop" data-title="Feedback Loop"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Feedback Loop</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_FEEDBACK_LOOP"><h3>Feedback Loop</h3><p class="requirement">INT 15 / magic_pool</p><p>Every continuation die actually generated by an offensive Magic attack restores 1 Magic to its caster, capped at 6 restored Magic per committed cast/attack event. Initial dice and unbridged weapon-only Boomchains never count.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and Magic-using AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 86</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_float_on" data-title="Float On"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Float On</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_FLOAT_ON"><h3>Float On</h3><p class="requirement">INT 15 / Magic pool</p><p>Once per airborne cycle, hold Space at the apex for a controllable float of up to 3.0 seconds, spending exactly 5 Magic per second. It ends on release, ground contact, exhaustion, or cap.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 87</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_grand_unified_theory" data-title="Grand Unified Theory"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Grand Unified Theory</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_GRAND_UNIFIED_THEORY"><h3>Grand Unified Theory</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / unowned Magic form</p><p>Immediately grants one deterministic distinct canonical Magic form without replacing later scheduled grants.</p><p class="actors">Cooperative Heroes only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 88</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_haste" data-title="Haste"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Haste</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_HASTE_1"><h3>Haste</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13 / Magic pool</p><p>Adds a dedicated rebindable Haste toggle whose default keyboard binding is H. Haste begins OFF. Pressing H while alive, player-controlled, and at positive Magic toggles Haste ON; pressing H again toggles it OFF. While Haste is ON and funded, HasteMovementMultiplier = 2.00 and applies to the actor&#x27;s resolved voluntary locomotion speed after ordinary walk/run/sprint mode, DEX movement scaling, MapOpenMovementMultiplier when applicable, and other compatible ordinary movement modifiers. Haste therefore doubles ordinary walking and ordinary Shift sprinting alike; it never replaces, consumes, disables, or changes access to the actor&#x27;s normal sprint. HasteMagicDrainRate = CurrentMapOpenMagicDrainRate, using the same personal WIS-scaled utility-Magic rate as map viewing. Magic regeneration is suppressed while Haste is actively draining. Haste and map viewing are independent sustained Magic consumers: at base Haste, if both are active simultaneously, TotalUtilityMagicDrainRate = CurrentMapOpenMagicDrainRate + HasteMagicDrainRate = 2 × CurrentMapOpenMagicDrainRate. Reaching 0 Magic immediately turns Haste OFF and returns locomotion to its ordinary legal speed; death or loss of player control likewise ends the active Haste state. A map force-close caused by damage or map-Magic exhaustion ends only the map state and its map-open movement bonus; it does not itself toggle Haste OFF if Haste still has positive Magic. Haste changes no jump velocity, Wall Jump, Cloud Step, Float On, Push/knockback, falling, projectile motion, or forced movement.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_HASTE_2"><h3>Mana Rush</h3><p class="requirement">INT 15 / requires Haste</p><p>Replaces Haste&#x27;s drain multiplier with HasteDrainMultiplier = 2/3 while preserving HasteMovementMultiplier = 2.00 for both walking and ordinary sprinting. HasteMagicDrainRate = CurrentMapOpenMagicDrainRate × 2/3 after the actor&#x27;s normal WIS utility-Magic scaling has already determined the map-equivalent rate. Map viewing remains a separate sustained consumer, so if Haste and the map are active together their legal rates add. All Haste toggle, normal-sprint preservation, regeneration-suppression, and zero-Magic termination rules remain unchanged.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_HASTE_3"><h3>Aether Drive</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / requires Mana Rush</p><p>Replaces Mana Rush&#x27;s drain multiplier with HasteDrainMultiplier = 1/3 while preserving HasteMovementMultiplier = 2.00 for both walking and ordinary sprinting. HasteMagicDrainRate = CurrentMapOpenMagicDrainRate × 1/3 after ordinary WIS utility-Magic scaling. Haste and map viewing remain independent sustained Magic consumers: if both are active simultaneously, each applies its own legal drain and the rates add; either one suppresses Magic regeneration while active. All other Haste toggle, normal-sprint preservation, and zero-Magic termination rules remain unchanged.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 89</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_mana_spring" data-title="Mana Spring"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Mana Spring</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_MANA_SPRING"><h3>Mana Spring</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13 / magic_pool</p><p>Whenever Magic reaches 0, the next time regeneration becomes legally permitted the actor receives a 1.50 multiplier to its already INT-scaled Magic regeneration for 4.0 seconds. The timer does not run and no regeneration occurs while the minimap or another regeneration-suppressing sustained effect remains active.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and Magic-using AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 90</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_map_movement" data-title="World Walker"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>World Walker</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_WORLD_WALKER_1"><h3>World Walker</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>While your personal minimap is legally open, ordinary movement speed is multiplied by 1.25. Only the highest rank applies; closes, lost access and exhausted Magic end the bonus. Does not modify jump velocity or forced movement.</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_GLOBETROTTER_2"><h3>Globetrotter</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>While your personal minimap is legally open, ordinary movement speed is multiplied by 1.50. Only the highest rank applies; closes, lost access and exhausted Magic end the bonus. Does not modify jump velocity or forced movement.</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_MIND_STRIDER_3"><h3>Mind Strider</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>While your personal minimap is legally open, ordinary movement speed is multiplied by 1.75. Only the highest rank applies; closes, lost access and exhausted Magic end the bonus. Does not modify jump velocity or forced movement.</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 91</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_quantum_cost" data-title="Quantum Mathematics"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Quantum Mathematics</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_QUANTUM_MATHEMATICS_1"><h3>Quantum Mathematics</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Offensive active Magic costs 11% less, rounded up with a minimum cost of 1. Highest rank replaces lower ranks. Utility costs, map drain, regeneration, damage and shield diversion are unchanged.</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_QUANTUM_MECHANICS_2"><h3>Quantum Mechanics</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Offensive active Magic costs 22% less, rounded up with a minimum cost of 1. Highest rank replaces lower ranks. Utility costs, map drain, regeneration, damage and shield diversion are unchanged.</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_QUANTUM_MASTERY_3"><h3>Quantum Mastery</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Offensive active Magic costs 33% less, rounded up with a minimum cost of 1. Highest rank replaces lower ranks. Utility costs, map drain, regeneration, damage and shield diversion are unchanged.</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 92</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_russian_asset" data-title="Russian Asset"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Russian Asset</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_RUSSIAN_ASSET"><h3>Russian Asset</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13 / Tetris access</p><p>Doubles all temporary HP overfill earned from qualifying Tetris line-clear rewards, so the baseline single/double/triple/quad rewards become +20/+60/+100/+160 HP, in both death Tetris and post-rescue/victory Tetris. DeathTetrisMaxSeconds increases from 60 to 120 seconds. The mandatory 20-second death/respawn lockout and the 20-second post-rescue/victory window remain unchanged, and F still respawns immediately whenever it is eligible.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled cooperative heroes with Tetris access</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 93</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_size_shifter" data-title="Size Shifter"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Size Shifter</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_SIZE_SHIFTER"><h3>Size Shifter</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13</p><p>Crouching continuously transforms toward absolute 0.33 scale over 3.0 seconds; releasing crouch reverses at the same rate toward the build&#x27;s ordinary target scale. Collision hull and traversal legality remain ordinary crouched values.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 94</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_summon_management" data-title="Middle Manager"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Middle Manager</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_MIDDLE_MANAGER"><h3>Middle Manager</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13 / Summon Form</p><p>Raises that Hero&#x27;s caster-specific MaxActiveSummons from the default 1 to 2. This is a cap replacement, not an additive +1 stack. It changes only the number of that caster&#x27;s own allied Seeker summons that may coexist; it does not alter Summon duration, Magic cost, placement range, Seeker attack behavior, inherited SummonMagicPayload, Content, damage, or AI behavior. If the caster is already at the cap, another Summon cast is illegal and spends no Magic rather than replacing an existing summon.</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_TASKMASTER"><h3>Taskmaster</h3><p class="requirement">INT 15 / Summon Form</p><p>Raises that Hero&#x27;s caster-specific MaxActiveSummons to 3, replacing the Middle Manager cap rather than stacking with it. All Summon cost, duration, placement, payload inheritance, Content, damage, AI, and lifecycle rules remain unchanged.</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_OVERLORD"><h3>Overlord</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / Summon Form</p><p>Raises that Hero&#x27;s caster-specific MaxActiveSummons to 4, replacing the Taskmaster cap rather than stacking with it. Four is the authored maximum unless a future explicit rule changes it. All other Summon rules remain unchanged.</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 95</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-mana_barrier" data-title="Mana Barrier"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Mana Barrier</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_MANA_BARRIER_1"><h3>Mana Barrier</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13</p><p>Sets ManaBarrierFeatDiversionFraction = 0.15. This feat family is unavailable to Wizard-class actors; it is the INT-gated HP-to-Magic diversion path for eligible non-Wizards. Uses continuous post-mitigation HP-to-Magic diversion, limited by CurrentMagic, at 1 Magic per HP.</p><p class="actors">Eligible non-Wizard heroes, human Soldiers, and Magic-using AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_MANA_BARRIER_2"><h3>Arcane Aegis</h3><p class="requirement">INT 15 / Mana Barrier</p><p>Replaces Mana Barrier and sets ManaBarrierFeatDiversionFraction = 0.30. This feat is unavailable to Wizard-class actors. Uses continuous post-mitigation HP-to-Magic diversion, limited by CurrentMagic, at 1 Magic per HP.</p><p class="actors">Eligible non-Wizard heroes, human Soldiers, and Magic-using AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_MANA_BARRIER_3"><h3>Mystic Bastion</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / Arcane Aegis</p><p>Replaces lower Mana Barrier ranks and sets ManaBarrierFeatDiversionFraction = 0.45. This feat is unavailable to Wizard-class actors. Uses continuous post-mitigation HP-to-Magic diversion, limited by CurrentMagic, at 1 Magic per HP.</p><p class="actors">Eligible non-Wizard heroes, human Soldiers, and Magic-using AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 96</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-str_bleed_proc" data-title="Bloodletter"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Bloodletter</h2><section class="entry" id="STR_BLEED_PROC_1"><h3>Bloodletter</h3><p class="requirement">STR 13</p><p>Sets BleedProcChance = 0.11 under the shared status-proc feat-family rules. On an eligible target-hit event, a successful proc creates exactly one Bleeding application attempt. Bloodletter is STR-governed for feat qualification, but Bleeding remains a canonical CON-resisted condition: the attacker&#x27;s CON sets BleedDC and the defender&#x27;s CON sets BleedSave. A successful save prevents Bleeding. If the authored attack already guarantees a Bleeding application attempt, skip the redundant Bloodletter-family proc roll.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="STR_BLEED_PROC_2"><h3>Deep Wounds</h3><p class="requirement">STR 15 / requires Bloodletter</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets BleedProcChance = 0.22 under the shared status-proc feat-family rules. On an eligible target-hit event, a successful proc creates exactly one Bleeding application attempt. Bloodletter is STR-governed for feat qualification, but Bleeding remains a canonical CON-resisted condition: the attacker&#x27;s CON sets BleedDC and the defender&#x27;s CON sets BleedSave. A successful save prevents Bleeding. If the authored attack already guarantees a Bleeding application attempt, skip the redundant Bloodletter-family proc roll.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="STR_BLEED_PROC_3"><h3>Exsanguinator</h3><p class="requirement">STR 17 / requires Deep Wounds</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets BleedProcChance = 0.33 under the shared status-proc feat-family rules. On an eligible target-hit event, a successful proc creates exactly one Bleeding application attempt. Bloodletter is STR-governed for feat qualification, but Bleeding remains a canonical CON-resisted condition: the attacker&#x27;s CON sets BleedDC and the defender&#x27;s CON sets BleedSave. A successful save prevents Bleeding. If the authored attack already guarantees a Bleeding application attempt, skip the redundant Bloodletter-family proc roll.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 97</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-str_crowbar_crush" data-title="Wrecking Bar"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Wrecking Bar</h2><section class="entry" id="STR_CROWBAR_CRUSH"><h3>Wrecking Bar</h3><p class="requirement">STR 17 / requires Walloper</p><p>Crowbar-caused wall slams gain one die while preserving the current authoritative wall-slam die class and explosion seal.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers with Crowbar/Long-Sword-family access</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 98</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-str_crowbar_damage" data-title="Bash"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Bash</h2><section class="entry" id="STR_CROWBAR_D6"><h3>Bash</h3><p class="requirement">STR 13</p><p>Crowbar-family base damage becomes universal exploding 1d6. Each successful nonlethal hit requests one 168-unit physical push.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers with Crowbar/Long-Sword-family access</p></section><section class="entry" id="STR_CROWBAR_D12"><h3>Walloper</h3><p class="requirement">STR 15 / requires Bash</p><p>Replaces Bash&#x27;s d6 with universal SUPER 1d12 while retaining its one 168-unit physical push.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers with Crowbar/Long-Sword-family access</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 99</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-str_melee_reach" data-title="Long Reach"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Long Reach</h2><section class="entry" id="STR_MELEE_REACH"><h3>Long Reach</h3><p class="requirement">STR 15 / melee-family access</p><p>Ordinary melee-family reach is multiplied by 1.25, after which the existing geometry trace remains authoritative. This cannot strike through walls, gates, floors, or other blocking architecture.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers with melee-family access</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 100</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-str_pusher" data-title="Pusher"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Pusher</h2><section class="entry" id="STR_KNOCKBACK_1"><h3>Pusher</h3><p class="requirement">STR 13</p><p>Eligible nonlethal ordinary weapon hits have a 25% chance to add 168 push before the shared STR push save. Successful procs start a 0.50-second attacker-target cooldown. Ordinary physical-push wall slams use 1d8 with classExplosionImmune.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an ordinary weapon capable of damaging a pushable hostile</p></section><section class="entry" id="STR_KNOCKBACK_2"><h3>Shover</h3><p class="requirement">STR 15 / requires Pusher</p><p>Eligible nonlethal ordinary weapon hits have a 50% chance to add 168 push before the shared STR push save. Successful procs start a 0.50-second attacker-target cooldown. Ordinary physical-push wall slams use 1d10 with classExplosionImmune.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an ordinary weapon capable of damaging a pushable hostile</p></section><section class="entry" id="STR_KNOCKBACK_3"><h3>Space Hog</h3><p class="requirement">STR 17 / requires Shover</p><p>Eligible nonlethal ordinary weapon hits have a 75% chance to add 168 push before the shared STR push save. Successful procs start a 0.50-second attacker-target cooldown. Ordinary physical-push wall slams use 1d12 SUPER exploding.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an ordinary weapon capable of damaging a pushable hostile</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 101</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-str_steamroller" data-title="Steamroller"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Steamroller</h2><section class="entry" id="STR_STEAMROLLER"><h3>Steamroller</h3><p class="requirement">STR 17 / requires an authored push-capable attack or effect</p><p>Whenever a push-tagged event credited to this actor reaches the shared STR push save, a successful PushSave applies 50% of SizeAdjustedPushDistance instead of the ordinary 0%; a failed PushSave still applies 100%. Steamroller does not create push where none exists, does not alter PushDC or PushSave, does not grant extra saves, and never bypasses PushImmune. Any resulting nonzero displacement continues through ordinary defender-side post-save multipliers, LOD.Pushback collision handling, and wall-slam/wall-crush rules.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an authored push-capable attack or effect</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 102</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_astral_reach" data-title="Astral Reach"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Astral Reach</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_ASTRAL_REACH"><h3>Astral Reach</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 15 / owns a Magic Form</p><p>Adds 2 cells to WIS-scaled Magic Form spatial dimensions.</p><p class="actors">Cooperative Heroes only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 103</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_attunement" data-title="Attunement"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Attunement</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_ATTUNEMENT"><h3>Attunement</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 17 / owns an elemental Magic attack</p><p>When an elemental Magic attack exploits a weakness, roll the weakness-bonus table twice and keep the more favorable bonus.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and eligible AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 104</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_breadcrumb_range" data-title="Surveyor"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Surveyor</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_SURVEYOR"><h3>Surveyor</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 13</p><p>Adds +4 BreadcrumbCells after the normal WIS formula without revealing topology forbidden by map degradation.</p><p class="actors">Heroes and human Soldiers with minimap access</p></section><section class="entry" id="WIS_CARTOGRAPHER"><h3>Cartographer</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 15 / requires Surveyor</p><p>Replaces Surveyor&#x27;s +4 with +8 BreadcrumbCells after the normal WIS formula; degradation and current-floor restrictions remain absolute.</p><p class="actors">Heroes and human Soldiers with minimap access</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 105</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_forceful_magic" data-title="Force Multiplier"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Force Multiplier</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_FORCEFUL_MAGIC"><h3>Force Multiplier</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 15 / magic_push</p><p>Actor-authored magic_push displacement is multiplied by 1.25. Force Shout is the initial intended beneficiary. Physical-push feats do not automatically stack unless a cross-system bridge makes the event eligible for both families.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with a Magic push</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 106</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_frugal_map" data-title="Frugal Cartography"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Frugal Cartography</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_FRUGAL_MAP"><h3>Frugal Cartography</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 15</p><p>Multiplies WIS-scaled minimap drain by 0.85, with final drain never below 3.0 Magic/second; Magic regeneration remains disabled while open.</p><p class="actors">Heroes and human Soldiers with minimap access</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 107</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_gps" data-title="GPS"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>GPS</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_GPS"><h3>GPS</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 17</p><p>Adds a private old-school synthetic GPS navigation assist with a dedicated rebindable toggle whose default keyboard binding is G. GPS starts enabled immediately when the feat is acquired. Acquisition displays a concise tooltip/system notice: GPS ENABLED — If it gets annoying, press G to turn it off. Press G again to turn it back on. Pressing the GPS action toggles the feature without spending Magic; every toggle plays a short electronic switch/chime and produces the ordinary bounded on-screen system notice GPS ON or GPS OFF. While enabled, GPS speaks after 1 second standing still without living enemies within 2 cells on the same floor, including enemies behind walls and human Soldiers. It repeats after a 4-second silence following each phrase. Movement, danger, combat or inactive states reset the trigger and cancel speech. Aim/facing may change while stationary. When triggered, GPS reads only the authoritative canonical route from the Hero&#x27;s current cell to the currently active progression objective and emits one short 2000s/early-2010s-style direction assembled from a small fixed synthetic/concatenative voice bank. Supported phrase families include TURN LEFT, TURN RIGHT, TURN AROUND, CONTINUE FORWARD, IN N SQUARES TURN LEFT/RIGHT, IN N SQUARES TAKE THE STAIRS UP/DOWN, TAKE THE STAIRS UP/DOWN, and YOU HAVE ARRIVED AT YOUR DESTINATION. N is derived from the contiguous legal route segment to the next turn, stair transition, or objective rather than guessed. GPS never invents a shortcut, predicts future progression stages, reveals enemies or loot, or performs a second pathfinding authority: it consumes the same canonical current-objective route used by ordinary navigation/breadcrumb logic. GPS is supplemental information and remains available even when lod_mapless 1 removes the visual minimap; it does not itself reveal a map or persistent route display. Active combat, death/spectating, staging, cutscenes, and other states where a navigation bark would be intrusive suspend the idle trigger. GPS has no Magic cost and does not alter Magic regeneration, BreadcrumbCells, movement, combat statistics, rewards, or objective logic.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 108</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_held_proc" data-title="Snaring"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Snaring</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_HELD_PROC_1"><h3>Snaring</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 13</p><p>Sets HeldProcChance = 0.11 under the shared status-proc feat-family rules. On a successful proc, the target makes exactly one ordinary WIS MagicSave against the attacker&#x27;s WIS-based MagicDC; failure applies canonical Held. This creates a Held attempt only and never bypasses the defender&#x27;s Wisdom.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="WIS_HELD_PROC_2"><h3>Binding</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 15 / requires Snaring</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets HeldProcChance = 0.22 under the shared status-proc feat-family rules. On a successful proc, the target makes exactly one ordinary WIS MagicSave against the attacker&#x27;s WIS-based MagicDC; failure applies canonical Held. This creates a Held attempt only and never bypasses the defender&#x27;s Wisdom.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="WIS_HELD_PROC_3"><h3>Entrapping</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 17 / requires Binding</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets HeldProcChance = 0.33 under the shared status-proc feat-family rules. On a successful proc, the target makes exactly one ordinary WIS MagicSave against the attacker&#x27;s WIS-based MagicDC; failure applies canonical Held. This creates a Held attempt only and never bypasses the defender&#x27;s Wisdom.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 109</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_hero_of_legend" data-title="Hero of Legend"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Hero of Legend</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_HERO_OF_LEGEND"><h3>Hero of Legend</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 15</p><p>At CurrentHP &gt;= min(100, MaxHP), a committed Crowbar-family primary swing launches one globally exclusive, nonrecursive glowing Crowbar projectile. It travels at Bio Blaster speed for max(1, WIS bonus) grid cells and deals non-elemental Magic damage with the current Crowbar die.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers with Crowbar/Long-Sword-family access</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 110</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_killer_instinct" data-title="Killer Instinct"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Killer Instinct</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_KILLER_INSTINCT"><h3>Killer Instinct</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 15</p><p>While controlled by a human and wielding an equipped damage-dealing weapon, Killer Instinct remains dormant unless at least two living hostile actors are simultaneously inside the player&#x27;s ordinary forward view and pass the same player-facing visibility/line-of-sight authority used for legal target identification. When that multi-hostile condition first becomes true and remains continuously true for 0.50 seconds, perform one target-priority evaluation; while it remains true, reevaluate no more than once every 1.00 second. If fewer than two valid hostiles remain, immediately clear the highlight and stop all Killer Instinct evaluation until the condition becomes true again; there is no general per-frame Think scan. Candidate discovery must reuse the existing visible/targetable hostile set or equivalent cached authority and may not iterate every world entity solely for this feat. For each valid candidate, compute a cheap deterministic EstimatedEffectiveDamagePerShot for one ordinary primary-fire trigger pull from the equipped weapon&#x27;s current authored attack profile, using current deterministic attacker/target modifiers and mean damage-die values; do not roll dice, simulate Boom chains, predict future status procs, or Monte Carlo attacks. EstimatedShotsToKill = max(1, ceil(CurrentHP / max(1, EstimatedEffectiveDamagePerShot))). If one or more candidates have EstimatedShotsToKill = 1, select the one with the greatest EstimatedEffectiveDamagePerShot - CurrentHP kill margin; otherwise select the candidate with the lowest EstimatedShotsToKill. Break any remaining tie by lower CurrentHP, then stable actor ID. Render one red outline/halo tightly around the selected hostile model. The outline is informational only: it grants no aim assist, targeting lock, damage, AI-priority change, extra detection range, through-wall awareness, or tracking after ordinary visibility is lost, and it clears immediately when the target dies or becomes invalid.</p><p class="actors">Human-controlled Heroes and Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 111</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_mind_over_matter" data-title="Mind Over Matter"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Mind Over Matter</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_MIND_OVER_MATTER"><h3>Mind Over Matter</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 17 / requires True Faith</p><p>While this feat is ready, the first incoming damage event tagged physical=true automatically receives PhysicalDamageReduction = max(0, WIS_MOD), applied once to the event&#x27;s aggregated physical damage after ordinary damage dice/Boom resolution, CON DamageResistancePerDie, source-side scaling, and elemental/identity modifiers, but before Arcane Shield HP-to-Magic diversion, lethal intercepts, and final HP loss. Never reduce damage below 0. After an eligible physical event consumes the ready state, roll MindOverMatterCooldownSeconds = 3d4 seconds and do not apply Mind Over Matter again until that cooldown expires. These three d4 timing dice are sealed, non-damage utility dice and never explode or inherit Rogue damage-die mastery, DEX BoomShift, Wizard magical Boom rules, weapon-specific explosion rules, or other attack-die modifiers. When the cooldown expires, Mind Over Matter becomes ready again. Magical-only events with physical=false do not consume the ready state. A mixed physical=true/magical=true event may receive True Faith&#x27;s magical reduction and, when Mind Over Matter is ready, Mind Over Matter&#x27;s physical reduction on the same resolved event; each applies once and final damage is clamped at 0. Mind Over Matter does not alter Push, wall-slam damage, hit-stun, status saves, MagicSave, or any non-damage physical effect.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 112</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_mute_proc" data-title="Hushing"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Hushing</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_MUTE_PROC_1"><h3>Hushing</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 13</p><p>Sets MuteProcChance = 0.11. On an eligible target-hit event under the common status-proc rules, a successful proc creates one mute-tagged application attempt using the ordinary attacker-WIS MagicDC and defender-WIS MagicSave formulas. Failure applies canonical Muted; success prevents it.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="WIS_MUTE_PROC_2"><h3>Silencing</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 15 / requires Hushing</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets MuteProcChance = 0.22. On an eligible target-hit event under the common status-proc rules, a successful proc creates one mute-tagged application attempt using the ordinary attacker-WIS MagicDC and defender-WIS MagicSave formulas. Failure applies canonical Muted; success prevents it.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="WIS_MUTE_PROC_3"><h3>Dead Air</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 17 / requires Silencing</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets MuteProcChance = 0.33. On an eligible target-hit event under the common status-proc rules, a successful proc creates one mute-tagged application attempt using the ordinary attacker-WIS MagicDC and defender-WIS MagicSave formulas. Failure applies canonical Muted; success prevents it.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 113</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_omniscience" data-title="Omniscience"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Omniscience</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_OMNISCIENCE"><h3>Omniscience</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 17</p><p>While controlled by a human, whenever this actor looks at or within six degrees of a visible monster through the shared near-look identification authority, render an Omniscience readout above that monster at the same presentation anchor used for player identity text. For an ordinary AI monster, the readout shows the monster&#x27;s canonical type/archetype name, current Combat Level, current class, and current Hit Points as CurrentHP/MaxHP. Example structure: Soldier • Level 21 • Fighter • HP 84/117. The values update live while the target remains valid. Omniscience is informational only: it grants no extra targeting range, no through-wall or off-screen awareness, no outline or tracking after look-away, and no combat/stat bonus. A human-controlled Soldier is still a monster for Omniscience purposes, but its existing HumanSoldierText remains the primary identity line; Omniscience appends the same Type/Level/Class/HP readout rather than replacing or hiding the controlling player&#x27;s identity. Non-monster world entities and cooperative Heroes do not receive this monster-stat readout.</p><p class="actors">Human Heroes and human Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 114</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_reckless_proc" data-title="Agitating"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Agitating</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_RECKLESS_PROC_1"><h3>Agitating</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 13</p><p>Sets RecklessProcChance = 0.11 under the shared status-proc feat-family rules. On a successful proc, the target makes exactly one ordinary WIS MagicSave against the attacker&#x27;s WIS-based MagicDC; failure applies canonical Reckless. This creates a Reckless attempt only and never bypasses the defender&#x27;s Wisdom.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="WIS_RECKLESS_PROC_2"><h3>Unhinging</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 15 / requires Agitating</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets RecklessProcChance = 0.22 under the shared status-proc feat-family rules. On a successful proc, the target makes exactly one ordinary WIS MagicSave against the attacker&#x27;s WIS-based MagicDC; failure applies canonical Reckless. This creates a Reckless attempt only and never bypasses the defender&#x27;s Wisdom.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="WIS_RECKLESS_PROC_3"><h3>Maddening</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 17 / requires Unhinging</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets RecklessProcChance = 0.33 under the shared status-proc feat-family rules. On a successful proc, the target makes exactly one ordinary WIS MagicSave against the attacker&#x27;s WIS-based MagicDC; failure applies canonical Reckless. This creates a Reckless attempt only and never bypasses the defender&#x27;s Wisdom.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 115</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_sixth_sense" data-title="Sixth Sense"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Sixth Sense</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_SIXTH_SENSE"><h3>Sixth Sense</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 13</p><p>Sixth Sense grants three personal perception effects. First, the owner can visually perceive any entity whose authoritative state includes invisible=true. Invisibility is a reusable shared entity-state primitive rather than a Watcher-specific exception: Watchers use it now, and future enemies, effects, or actors may use the same state. An invisible entity is rendered only for the owning client as a clearly readable translucent silhouette/outline at its true current world position whenever that entity would otherwise satisfy ordinary world visibility and line-of-sight rules if invisibility were ignored. Second, Sixth Sense grants Nearby Hostile Sense: every living hostile entity on the owner&#x27;s current floor whose cell-coordinate distance is within 2 grid cells is rendered to that owner as a readable through-geometry outline even when intervening walls or props block line of sight. For this sensor, NearbyCellDistance = max(abs(enemyCellX-ownerCellX), abs(enemyCellY-ownerCellY)); the effect applies when NearbyCellDistance &lt;= 2 and floorId matches. This local 5x5-cell neighborhood intentionally ignores wall connectivity and closed-gate edges for perception only. Invisible hostiles within that neighborhood are also revealed by the same outline. Third, Sixth Sense grants Watcher Motion Sense: whenever a living Watcher is in its authoritative moving/locomotion state, each Sixth Sense owner on the same floor receives a private 3D positional Watcher movement sound attached to that Watcher&#x27;s true current position. This cue plays whether the Watcher is visible or invisible and does not require line of sight; ordinary spatial attenuation provides direction and proximity, so a distant Watcher does not become an all-floor audio beacon. The cue starts when authoritative Watcher locomotion begins and stops when locomotion stops, the Watcher dies/despawns, the player changes floor, or Sixth Sense is no longer active. The movement sound is transmitted/rendered only for eligible Sixth Sense owners; players without the feat receive no such sound event. These effects create no minimap marker, breadcrumb, directional arrow, nameplate through the world, aim assistance, target lock, ballistic permission through geometry, AI aggro knowledge, or interaction permission. Sixth Sense never changes an entity&#x27;s invisible state, cloak duration, AI/state machine, collision, targetability rules, or visibility to any other player; players without the feat perceive the entity normally. The server authoritatively determines feat ownership, invisible state, hostility, floor, cell coordinates, and Watcher locomotion state; owning clients render only authorized silhouettes and private Watcher movement audio. FeatDirector may offer Sixth Sense whenever the actor is an eligible cooperative hero; Watchers or any other invisibility-using enemy need not currently be present because the 2-cell hostile-sense effect is independently useful.</p><p class="actors">Cooperative Heroes</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 116</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_spatial_awareness" data-title="Spatial Awareness"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Spatial Awareness</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_SPATIAL_AWARENESS"><h3>Spatial Awareness</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 15</p><p>Warns about visible hostile monsters behind you and directly to either side. RearRangeCells = max(1, WIS_MOD), without Astral Reach. Quantize horizontal facing to the nearest cardinal maze direction. The rear footprint remains three cells wide for depths 1 through RearRangeCells: directly behind, plus one cell on either side of each rear cell. Add a single-cell-wide ray directly left and directly right from the player&#x27;s current cell, each extending SideRangeCells = ceil(RearRangeCells / 2). No forward cells or other floors qualify. Closed walls, closed gates and ordinary blocking geometry still block detection. Retain the selected monster while it qualifies; otherwise choose by shortest footprint depth, then smallest absolute lateral offset, then stable actor identity. On acquisition or replacement after the prior selection ceases to qualify, name the monster in a private BEHIND YOU, LEFT or RIGHT notice in the live die-readout and Die Log, play a clearly audible alert, and briefly show a violet directional light toward its position at detection. The light is a transient directional notification, not an enemy outline, minimap marker or persistent tracker. Do not repeat the alert while the same selected monster remains qualified. No target lock, aim assist, combat bonus, through-wall detection or AI behavior change.</p><p class="actors">Human Heroes and human Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 117</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-wis_spellward" data-title="Spellward"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Spellward</h2><section class="entry" id="WIS_SPELLWARD"><h3>Spellward</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 13</p><p>Adds +2 to Magic Saves against explicitly resistible magical effects.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="WIS_SPELLBREAKER"><h3>Spellbreaker</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 15 / requires Spellward</p><p>Replaces the lower-rank Magic Save bonus with +4 against explicitly resistible magical effects.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="WIS_SPELLBANE"><h3>Spellbane</h3><p class="requirement">WIS 17 / requires Spellbreaker</p><p>Replaces the lower-rank Magic Save bonus with +]====]
